      \field{abstract}{Reinforcing steels with a strength of 600 MPa have the potential to significantly reduce embodied carbon in structures. When designing reinforced concrete elements for ultimate strength, using these higher strength steels can save up to 17 per cent of material by mass compared to the standard 500 MPa grade steels. This saving is due to the smaller crosssectional area required. However, one challenge is the longer development lengths mandated by the Australian concrete structures standard (AS 3600), which currently limit these savings.}
